From 57577fe6ca95848d83702df765f3d34ced233dcb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 13:26:55 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 11/14] mmc: add a SigmaStar SSD20xD SD host controller driver

New driver for the SD host ("SDIO v5") of SigmaStar SSD20xD
(Infinity2M) SoCs. The register programming follows the vendor HAL that
ships, byte-identical, in the Gustard R26 kernel: every command rewrites
the register block, data moves by ADMA, reads run as one job and writes
as a command job followed by a data job, CMD12 is sent by hand, R1b
waits on BUSY_DET_ON/BUSY_END, and the bogus response CRC error on R3
is cleared. The ERR_STS interrupt is never enabled.

The MIU write pipe flush the vendor does after building the ADMA table
is what wmb() already does on MStar v7 (ARM_HEAVY_MB/l3bridge).

Tested on the Gustard R26: byte-exact reads and writes, ext4 rootfs.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/mmc/host/Kconfig      |   8 +
 drivers/mmc/host/Makefile     |   1 +
 drivers/mmc/host/sstar-sdio.c | 702 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 711 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/mmc/host/sstar-sdio.c

